        "WebTrackingSummary",
        "WebTrackingSummaryDemo",
        "WebTrackingPageSummary",
        "WebTrackingPageSummaryDemo",
        "WebTrackingPurchaseSummary",
        "WebTrackingPurchaseSummaryDemo",
        "WebTrackingInteractionsSummary",
        "WebTrackingInteractionsSummaryDemo"
      ],
      "note": "The vendor docs name no row ID for these grids, so each key was chosen from the grid’s row grain: its own IDs, dimensions and event dates, never user_id (the tenant’s optional remote ID). Every part of a composite key must always be populated, because a row with an empty key part cannot be stored. MailingActivity is keyed on mailing_instance_ID alone because the docs define calculation_date as the stats’ as-of time. Known merge risks: opt-outs from several interests at the same instant (MailingActivityOptout omits Interest_ID, which whole-list opt-outs likely lack), and several SKUs bought on one page at one timestamp (SubscriberWebTracking). Unverified until a live sync: a non-unique key silently merges rows, so confirm uniqueness on the first one."
    },
    "disabled": {
      "objects": [
        "EmailBlockStatus",
        "ScoringSummary",
        "ScoringSummaryDemo"
      ],
      "note": "No usable key: EmailBlockStatus is the brand’s current email block, and ScoringSummary rows are scoring groups identified only by a description."
    }
  },
  "WriteContract": {
    "transport": "PostInformzMessage envelope carrying an ActionRequest document",
    "identity": {
      "mode": "readback",
      "grid": "subscriber",
      "conditions": [
        "user_id",
        "email"
      ],
      "key": "subscriber_id",
      "preWriteReadback": "user_id EQ ID AND email EQ Email, NumberOfRows 2: one row returns its subscriber_id without posting; zero posts Subscribe then reads back; more than one gives Success:false",
      "cite": "360032692392 (response has no subscriber_id); 360032692332 (user_id and email both Conditional=True); 360032692452 (multiple Conditions conjunctive); 360032697272 (match key undocumented)",
      "postWriteReadback": "After a posted Subscribe, read back with the same Conditions (user_id EQ ID AND email EQ Email), NumberOfRows 2: exactly one row returns ExternalID = its subscriber_id; zero rows, a fault, or a row without subscriber_id returns Success:false with no ExternalID and StatusCode null (non-403), so the engine counts RecordsErrored and holds the watermark. Never return Success:true with an empty ExternalID. The keyed AddOrUpdateSubscribers re-send on the next push is safe because the pre-write read-back short-circuits on a row that already exists."
    },
    "interestActionPolicy": "AddOrUpdateSubscribers only; no list-replacing action is emitted",
    "connectionSettings": [
      "SubscribeInterestNames",
      "SubscribeFieldDefinitions"
    ],
    "faults": {
      "codesArticle": 360044601092,
      "codesDocumentedAs": "some possible; no per-code meaning documented",
      "classification": {
        "authOrPrecondition": [
          "InvalidCredentialsException",
          "BrandNotFoundException",
          "ValidUserNotFoundException",
          "NoAvailableIPAddressException",
          "SystemAccessException",
          "ConfigurationErrorException"
        ],
        "requestDefect": [
          "InvalidDocumentException",
          "UnknownActionException",
          "InvalidDataFormatException",
          "UnexpectedInputException",
          "InvalidMessageException",
          "NoNameSpaceSpecifiedException",
          "InsufficientDataToCreateSubscriberException",
          "InsufficientInformationToCompleteActionException",
          "ConflictingInformationException",
          "MismatchedTargetGroupsException",
          "MultipleDefaultTargetGroupsException",
          "ItemNotFoundException",
          "InvalidGridCategoryException",
          "UnknownRequestException"
        ],
        "retryable": [
          "transport-level only (HTTP 429/503, connection errors); no ActionRequest fault code is documented as retryable"
        ]
      },
      "classificationNote": "Connector design decision over documented code names (the vendor does not classify them); all 20 codes named in 360044601092 are classified. InvalidGridCategoryException and UnknownRequestException fire on the identity read-back GridRequest (not on the ActionRequest) and surface exactly like any request defect: Success:false with code and reason verbatim, StatusCode per statusCodePolicy, no per-code retry.",
      "successParsing": "Status plus Message counts plus InvalidSubscribers; never rely on SubscriberCounts (360032692392)",
      "statusCodePolicy": {
        "rule": "No ActionRequest or GridRequest fault ever sets StatusCode 403. The IntegrationEngine treats 403 as a permanent skip and advances the push watermark, which would silently lose the change; 403 is reserved for a permanently read-only object.",
        "authOrPrecondition": "StatusCode 401 or null (InvalidCredentials, BrandNotFound, ValidUserNotFound, NoAvailableIPAddress, SystemAccess, ConfigurationError): Success:false, the engine counts the record errored and holds the watermark, so the push is retried.",
        "requestDefect": "StatusCode 400 or 422 or null: Success:false with code and reason verbatim; counted errored, watermark held.",
        "transport": "HTTP 429 and 503 and connection errors are retryable and non-403.",
        "test": "A connector unit test asserts StatusCode !== 403 for every classified code and for the transport cases.",
        "cite": [
          360044601092
        ]
      }
    },
    "residuals": [
      {
        "gap": "AddOrUpdateSubscribers match key (Email+Remote ID vs Email)",
        "safeDefault": "pre-write read-back so correctness does not depend on the key",
        "cite": 360032697272
      },
      {
        "gap": "Whether Subscribe can change an email",
        "safeDefault": "never push an email change; an update whose email differs from the stored read value is refused (Success:false)",
        "cite": 360032697272
      },
      {
        "gap": "InterestDetails required on Subscribe",
        "safeDefault": "always send InterestDetails with AddOrUpdateSubscribers; InterestNames only when the connection configures them",
        "cite": 360032692392
      },
      {
        "gap": "FieldDefinitions per Field@element and DataType values",
        "safeDefault": "one FieldDefinition per Field sent, DataType from connection config (default String); no Field elements unless configured",
        "cite": 360032692392
      },
      {
        "gap": "InvalidSubscribers child shape",
        "safeDefault": "fail the record when Status is not success, the Message invalid-address count > 0, or InvalidSubscribers has any child; read-back is the final arbiter",
        "cite": 360032692392
      },
      {
        "gap": "ActionRequest fault code meanings",
        "safeDefault": "any fault -> Success:false verbatim, no per-code retry",
        "cite": 360044601092
      },
      {
        "gap": "Zero rows (or a fault) on the read-back after a posted Subscribe",
        "safeDefault": "Success:false with no ExternalID and a non-403 StatusCode; the record is re-sent on the next push",
        "cite": 360032692392
      },
      {
        "gap": "Subscriber grid read-back on user_id EQ ID AND email EQ Email (both Conditional=True, conjunctive) is documented but never exercised against the real endpoint (credential posture B): mock-proven only",
        "safeDefault": "One live one-record push with a credential is required before the write path is relied on",
        "cite": [
          360032692332,
          360032692452
        ]
      }
    ],
    "articleIds": [
      360032692392,
      360032692072,
      360032692332,
      360032692452,
      360032697272
    ],
    "writeGuard": {
      "object": "Subscriber",
      "appliesTo": [
        "CreateRecord",
        "UpdateRecord",
        "DeleteRecord"
      ],
      "evaluatedBefore": "building any ActionRequest document or issuing the identity read-back",
      "rules": [
        {
          "id": "delete-unsupported",
          "op": "DeleteRecord",
          "when": "always (SupportsDelete=false)",
          "sends": "nothing",
          "result": "Success:false"
        },
        {
          "id": "empty-attributes",
          "op": [
            "CreateRecord",
            "UpdateRecord"
          ],
          "when": "Attributes holds no field named in writeActions.<op>.elements and no connection-configured Field element; an MJ delete that reaches the create or update branch arrives this way",
          "sends": "nothing",
          "result": "Success:false"
        },
        {
          "id": "required-element-missing",
          "op": "CreateRecord",
          "when": "a writeActions.create.requiredElements element maps to a field that is absent, null or blank in Attributes",
          "sends": "nothing",
          "result": "Success:false naming the element"
        },
        {
          "id": "required-element-unresolved",
          "op": "UpdateRecord",
          "when": "a writeActions.update.requiredElements element is still absent, null or blank after resolving it from Attributes, else GetRecord(subscriber_id)",
          "sends": "no ActionRequest; the GetRecord read is the only request",
          "result": "Success:false naming the element"
        }
      ],
      "whenFired": {
        "Success": false,
        "StatusCode": null,
        "neverPosts": [
          "Subscribe",
          "Optout",
          "Unsubscribe"
        ]
      },
      "resultBasis": "Success:false rather than a silent no-op, so an MJ change that cannot be written (including an MJ delete of this object) shows as a failed record; StatusCode stays null because the vendor documents none for these cases",
      "reason": "Subscribe requires both of its required elements (360032692392), so a call missing either cannot form a valid document. Delete is unsupported (WriteScope.deleteDecision), and Optout/Unsubscribe are out-of-scope consent changes; Unsubscribe without an ID acts on the email alone (360032692392), so no incomplete or delete-routed call may fall back to one. With SupportsDelete=false the integration engine hands an MJ delete (no field values) to UpdateRecord when a record map exists and to CreateRecord when none exists.",
      "articleIds": [
        360032692392,
        360032692332
      ]
    }
  }
}'
